<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0038/e_0059/normalization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/EntityNormalization> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0038/tu_0001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Amiodarone\nDecreases sinus node frequency, prolongs QT interval\na\nPVC, VT, VF\n200–400 mg\nLoading dose: 600–1200 mg/24 h 8–10 days.\n(Loading dose: 5 mg/kg in 20 min–2 h, 2–3 times in 24 h, then 600–1200 mg/24 h 8–10 days)\nCardiac:\nBradycardia, TdP (infrequent)\nExtracardiac:\nPhotosensitivity, corneal deposits, hypothyroidism, hyperthyroidism, pulmonary toxicity, hepatotoxicity, polyneuropathy, skin discoloration\nPrecautions:\nSinus node dysfunction, severe AV conduction disturbances, hyperthyroidism\nOther considerations:\nCan be used in patients with heart failure. Increases the risk of myopathy when used with statins" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0038/na_0005> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasParameterEntity> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_d1710bde778e9e1be7f11ed2fef05ae0e7ef558d8677a37c27ae7f454230f712_n0038/e_0085> .
